  "question": {
    "text": "If $f(x)=f(a-x)$ then $\\int_0^a x f(x) d x$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ktm2I",
      "text": "$\\int_0^a f(x) d x$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AGubc",
      "text": "$\\frac{a^2}{2} \\int_0^{\\mathrm{a}} \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x}) \\mathrm{dx}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tcHaD",
      "text": "$\\frac{a}{2} \\int_0^a f(x) d x$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "y1UkG",
      "text": "$-\\frac{a}{2} \\int_0^{\\mathrm{a}} f(x) d x$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints : $f(x)=f(a-x), I=\\int_0^a x f(x) d x=\\int_0^a(a-x) f(a-x) d x$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\int_0^a(a-x) f(x) d x=a \\int_0^a f(x) d x-I \\\\\n& \\therefore 2 I=a \\int_0^a f(x) d x \\Rightarrow I=\\frac{a}{2} \\int_0^a f(x) d x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
